  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the western districts of Toulon, near the Pont du Las, the Parc des Cèdres offers a green space of 0.66 hectare (about 6,600 m² according to the city of Toulon), with a playground and a boules court in addition to the dog area. A modest-sized neighbourhood park.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park is among the dog areas in the municipal document "Toulon, ville amie des chiens" (published online in November 2025), which reminds visitors that a leash and picking up waste are compulsory throughout the municipality, including in dog areas. The document gives no details on opening times or the size of the dog area; the park page on toulon.fr gives opening daily 9am-7pm. A 2020 city press release on the renovation describes a dog area running "around the edge of the park", i.e. along the paths, in a densely wooded park of 7,000 m²; the city now gives 6,600 m². The park is labelled a LPO bird refuge by the city, one more reason to keep dogs out of the flowerbeds.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: a neighbourhood spot for a green break, with no need to plan a whole afternoon.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The western districts of Toulon and the Pont du Las area are right next door, handy for fitting this break into an urban walk. For more room to run, the municipal list names other dog areas (parc de la Florane, parc Raoulx, jardin Alexandre 1er, parc des Lices with an agility zone, parc des plages du Mourillon). Dogs are also welcome on the Faron massif and ride the cable car free, according to the city.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> the exact size of the dog area, which the municipal list does not give; upkeep (a March 2026 press article criticises the size and upkeep of some of the city's dog areas, without naming this park).</p>
    </div>

